mpms_warn_dofquantity.out
Warning test: a variable's declared field disagrees with the dofs it occupies.
# The field a Variable represents and the dofs it lives on are independent declarations, so they
# can contradict each other. Here the displacement field is stored on V_u/V_v, which conventionally
# carry velocity. That is legitimate -- a deck may place a field on an unconventional dof, and the
# Non-isothermal decks do -- so it warns and runs rather than failing. Without the warning a stale
# or mistyped "quantity" changes what a variable means with no diagnostic at all, and surfaces far
# away as an unsupported-material-mode error inside a state operator.
# 
test nsteps 1 nvariables 2 nterms 2 nintegrals 2 lhsterms 1 1 rhsterms 1 2 nmodules 0
Variable name "u" interpolation "feilin" type 1 quantity "Displacements" size 2 dofs 2 7 8 # displacement 
Variable name "w" interpolation "feilin" type 1 quantity "Displacements" size 2 dofs 2 7 8 # test function
BTSigmaTerm 1 variable "u"  testvariable "w" mmode 6
NTfTerm 2 variable "u" testvariable "w" mmode 6 flux 2 1. 0.
Integral 1 domain 1 set 1 term 1
Integral 2 domain 1 set 2 term 2
#
domain HeatTransfer
outputmanager tstep_all dofman_all element_all
ndofman 4 nelem 2 nbc 2 ncrosssect 1 nic 0 nltf 2 nmat 1 nset 4
node 1 coords 3 0.            0.           0.
node 2 coords 3 1.0           0.           0.
node 3 coords 3 1.0           1.0          0.
node 4 coords 3 0.0           1.0          0.
#
q1 1 nodes 4 1 2 3 4 mat 1 crosssect 1
l1 2 nodes 2 2 3     mat 1 crosssect 1
#
simplecs 1 thick 1.0
isole 1 d 1 e 1 n 0.3 talpha 1.
# x-displacement
boundarycondition 1 loadtimefunction 1 set 3 values 1 0   dofs 1 7 
# y-displacement
boundarycondition 2 loadtimefunction 1 set 4 values 1 0   dofs 1 8 
#
#
constantfunction 1 f(t) 1
PiecewiseLinFunction 2 nPoints 4 t 4 -10. 0. 1. 5. f(t) 4 0. 0. 1.0 1.0 
set 1 elements 1 1
# 
set 2 elements 1 2 
# x-bc
set 3 nodes 2 1 4
# y-bc
set 4 nodes 1 1
